ntineoplastic agent, is explicitly listed as a BCRP substrate, making it susceptible to increased systemic exposure when co-administered with BCRP inhibitors like NW-1689. This elevates the risk of toxicity, including cardiotoxicity and myelosuppression. Additionally, 米托蒽醌 is linked to the adverse reaction '多药耐药', reflecting challenges in maintaining therapeutic efficacy due to upregulation of efflux transporters like P-glycoprotein (P-gp) and BCRP. Despite research into agents that downregulate these transporters, no clinically satisfactory solutions have emerged [Data: Entities (7642); Relationships (15003, 26313)]. This dual vulnerability—both as a victim of resistance mechanisms and a target of pharmacokinetic interactions—complicates its clinical use.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"乳腺癌 appears both as a disease indication and a side effect in specific populations\",\n            \"explanation\": \"While 乳腺癌 is primarily referenced here as a side effect (classified under SideEffect entity type), it is specifically noted to apply to the 绝经期后 population, based on structured evidence indicating its association with certain antineoplastic therapies in postmenopausal women. This contrasts with its role as a therapeutic target for drugs like 拉帕替尼 in HER2-positive cases. The dual context—disease vs. adverse outcome—highlights the importance of population stratification in risk-benefit assessments [Data: Entities (15366, 14862); Relationships (5073)]. Regulatory and clinical decisions must carefully distinguish between drug-induced carcinogenic risk and therapeutic intervention for existing malignancy.\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"氯氧喹 impacts liver function, warranting monitoring during use\",\n            \"explanation\": \"氯氧喹 is associated with effects on 肝功能, with clinical guidance recommending regular monitoring of liver enzymes and blood counts during prolonged use. Although limited data is available (only three source